    "insert": "\nThe motivation has the goal to catch reader's interest, explain specific problem and in which domain it occurs and also how the problem is currently handled. It should also state research questions explicitly and precisely.\nYour RQs are well structured. \nYour hook and the explanation of the problem could benefit from a more detailed explanation, and also concentrating on the core aspects of your study from the beginning. \nYou also did not really state a problem which your work wants to tackle.\n\n\nApproach\nIn the approach, the goal is to explain current State of the Art and explain the research gap that would further improve the existing work. It should also state your methods, how they relate to your RQs and what their challenges and limitations are. \nIn the methods, it's good that you explain exactly what you want to measure and also how you structure your experiment in groups. However, a more detailed description about the interaction the participants will have (e.g. do they have to solve a task, do they get any instructions) would further improve this section. \n\n\n"
